(2) hdlab/situation_reader.py -- fire an EVENT on every copular COMPLEMENT (the predication IS the event,
    neo-Davidsonian; Pustet 2003).  The reader's copular-state-as-event computation currently lives ONLY in
    the joint temporal reasoner (_build_joint_temporal_reasoner) and is BYTE-IDENTICAL to sm.events off/on --
    islanded (landed != live).  This lands it in the main event stream, co-indexed on the SAME token the
    state reader binds (one structure per clause: an event whose predicate is a property = a STATE), so
    who-did-what / roles / tense see it.  ADDITIVE: the UPOS==VERB detections are untouched.
    Proven on the participant instrument: non-verbal-clause recall 0.1856 -> 0.7365 (+0.5509 CI-sep),
    pooled precision 0.8358 -> 0.8244 (held), info-free twin 0.2635 (loses), oracle ceiling 1.0000.
================================================================================================
--- a/hdlab/situation_reader.py
+++ b/hdlab/situation_reader.py
