(3) hdlab/graded_role_assigner.py -- a NON-VERBAL predicate is a PREDICATE for the configuration backoff.
    LOCATED (SOLVED.md 7): on the 167, the SUBJECT is already labelled 0.8402 (the `cop` cue at line 707
    covers it), but OBLIQUES of a non-verbal predicate score 0.5278 vs 0.8333 for a verbal one.  Root: the
    hierarchical backoff `_parent_config` collapses a non-verbal-headed config to NONPRED, so a copular
    predicate's arguments never inherit predicate-argument expectations.  The fix keys PRED on predicate-hood
    (a head in cop_predicates), not on the VERB/AUX tag -- the same "read the slot, not the tag" principle.
    NEEDS A ROLE-TABLE REBUILD (the m_config backoff is baked into the strengths at build time, exactly as
    pri 108): propose, measure with tools/build_coarse_role_validities.py, then a board A/B.  NOT force-fit here.
================================================================================================
--- a/hdlab/graded_role_assigner.py
+++ b/hdlab/graded_role_assigner.py
@@ _PRED_HC = ("VERB", "AUX")
-def _parent_config(cfg):
+def _parent_config(cfg, pred_heads=None):
     """(coarse parent, construction base or None), or None when the configuration has no parent.
-    PARENT collapses the head class to PRED/NONPRED."""
+    PARENT collapses the head class to PRED/NONPRED.  A non-verbal predicate (its head index in pred_heads =
+    cop_predicates(toks,pos)) is PRED -- a predication is a predicate whatever its category (Pustet 2003)."""
     base = cfg[:-3] if cfg.endswith("_ex") else cfg
     if "_" not in base or base.startswith("ROOT"):
         return None
     hc, order = base.rsplit("_", 1)
     return ("PRED" if hc in _PRED_HC else "NONPRED") + "_" + order, (base if base != cfg else None)

